# Claude Code local settings (machine-specific, not project config)
.claude/

# Moderator build. These files exist only on the two machines that hold a key; the hooks they
# implement are partial methods, so an ordinary build erases both them and every call to them.
# Shipping code that can ban players to thirty thousand people is a risk with no upside - the
# safest version of it is the one that was never in the release.
UI/PluginUI.Admin*.cs
Core/Admin*.cs
# ...except the hook declarations, which MUST stay in the repo: they are what the ordinary build
# compiles (to nothing), and a missing partial declaration is a build error for everybody else.
!UI/PluginUI.AdminHooks.cs
